 "notes": "The evidence supports about 12 core cafés, not 20: Malmö has few café institutions that outlive a decade, and most of the brainstorm names failed. Hollandia is open (job ads July 2026) and is the one unquestionable pick. Not found or not cafés: Café Siesta (Siesta at Hjorttackegatan is a bar/restaurant), Glassfabriken/Glassbaren (only Lilla Glassfabriken exists), Café Bulten, Café Kontoret, a Pildammsteatern/Pildammsparken café (Malmö stad mentions a café at Margaretapaviljongen since 1935 but OSM has no café there; Bloom in the Park is a restaurant), Ebbas Fik (no trace online, probably closed; Ebbas hus is a museum). Pronto (way/1091108905) is a brand-tagged café near Lilla torg, not verified, left out. Konditori Lundagård is in Lund, outside. Mormors Bageri is a Lund bakery that has been in Malmö for some years: put under everything. Konditori Katarina (since 1959) is a local chain with 6+ branches; I made the Triangeln branch core (Wikivoyage) and dropped the two Hamngatan entries. The owner should decide whether a chain belongs in core at all. Gateau, St. Jakobs, Köld, Augusta, Coffee Square and Le Croissant are local chains: one branch kept or all dropped. Ribersborgs Kallbadhus (its café) is dropped because the bath is already in the game. Siri's Conditori (Södra Förstadsgatan 88) claims more than 70 years: a core candidate if the owner knows it. 'Lilla Pang' (Nobelvägen 44A) is now Bröd & Vänner according to OSM's other tags. Kafé Sisko is the Moderna Museet café. Café 2000 (Kaptensgatan, since 2000) is a salad lunch café: everything."
}
